From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:40:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the open lock opens a small modal -- the switch and
 Advanced
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Operator ask of 2026-11-23 (item 15): clicking the lock of an agent started
outside the jail opened the whole Agent Sandbox page -- folders, hosts,
limits, host view, capabilities -- when all the operator wanted was to turn
the jail on for this project. The decision (2026-11-24): before the jail is
on, the lock shows only this project's on/off switch, plus "Advanced…" for
the full page.

AgentJailQuickModal (agent_jail_quick_modal.rs) is a workspace modal with
the project's path, the switch "Run agents in ai-jail for this project" and
Advanced. The switch writes through agent_sandbox::confirm::
set_project_enabled -- the page's own path: only `enabled` changes, and
turning it off asks first -- and reads the setting of now as the lock does
(launch::jailed_on_next_start), redrawn on every settings change. Its hint
says the change applies on a restart; the lock then turns amber and a click
restarts, as since §6.50. Advanced opens the page and closes the modal.

render_jail_status_button takes `on_open`, what a click does when nothing is
pending; the thread view passes the modal only for Reason::Off. A jail
already on keeps opening the page, a pending change keeps the restart, and
a missing ai-jail keeps the lock disabled.

Logs: agent_sandbox event=quick_modal_toggle on=<bool>.

Tests: agent_jail_quick_modal_tests.rs -- the open lock opens the modal and
not the page, Advanced opens the page and closes it, and the switch follows
a setting saved elsewhere. agent_jail_status_closed_lock_opens_the_agent_
sandbox_page still holds for a jail that is on.
---

